Phase 3 — 5-Step Questionnaire Flow
Goal: Build a multi-step questionnaire with radio-button selections and back navigation. The answers will be used to filter products in the Playground.

Files to Create
File	Purpose
app/dashboard/employee/questionnaire/page.jsx	Server wrapper
components/employee/QuestionnaireFlow.jsx	Client component — multi-step form
Questionnaire Structure
Step	Question	Options (Radio — single select)
Q1	What's the occasion?	Wedding, Festival, Daily Wear, Gifting, Party
Q2	Select material	Gold, Silver, Diamond, Platinum, Artificial
Q3	What are you drawn to?	Traditional, Modern, Minimalist, Statement, Fusion
Q4	Jewel type	Necklaces, Rings, Bangles, Earrings, Pendants, View All (= all 5 selected)
Q5	What weight are you looking for?	Light (0–5g), Medium (5–15g), Heavy (15–30g), Statement (30g+)
Implementation Details
QuestionnaireFlow.jsx:

useState for currentStep (0–4) and answers object
Each step renders a question title + radio button options (only one selectable)
Back button on every step (except step 0) → decrements currentStep
Next button → increments currentStep
On final step submit → encode answers as query params and navigate to:
/dashboard/employee/playground?occasion=wedding&material=gold&style=traditional&type=necklaces&weight=light
Clean, card-based UI with progress indicator (step dots or progress bar)
