Phase 6 — Database Schema: Orders Table + APIs
Goal: Create the orders table in Supabase and build all CRUD APIs needed for the full order lifecycle.

IMPORTANT

This phase MUST be completed before Phases 5 and 7 can work. Run the SQL in Supabase Dashboard → SQL Editor.

SQL Migration to Create
File	Purpose
ORDERS_TABLE.sql	Full schema + RLS policies for the orders system
Database Schema
sql
CREATE TABLE public.orders (
  id              UUID DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() PRIMARY KEY,
  
  -- Parties
  product_id      UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.products(id),
  employee_id     UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.employees(id),
  retailer_id     UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.retailers(id),
  wholesaler_id   UUID NOT NULL REFERENCES public.wholesalers(id),
  
  -- Order Info
  customization_note  TEXT,
  rejection_reason    TEXT,
  
  -- Status Lifecycle
  status          TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'pending'
                  CHECK (status IN (
                    'pending',        -- Employee sent request, waiting for wholesaler
                    'accepted',       -- Wholesaler accepted
                    'rejected',       -- Wholesaler rejected (with reason)
                    'in_production',  -- Wholesaler marks as in production
                    'packed',         -- Wholesaler marks as packed
                    'dispatched',     -- Wholesaler marks as dispatched
                    'received',       -- Employee marks as received
                    'completed'       -- Final state
                  )),
  
  -- Timestamps
  created_at      TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now(),
  accepted_at     TIMESTAMPTZ,
  rejected_at     TIMESTAMPTZ,
  production_at   TIMESTAMPTZ,
  packed_at       TIMESTAMPTZ,
  dispatched_at   TIMESTAMPTZ,
  received_at     TIMESTAMPTZ,
  completed_at    TIMESTAMPTZ,
  updated_at      TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT now()
);
-- Indexes
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_employee   ON public.orders(employee_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_wholesaler ON public.orders(wholesaler_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_retailer   ON public.orders(retailer_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_orders_status     ON public.orders(status);
-- RLS
ALTER TABLE public.orders ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
-- Employees can see their own orders
CREATE POLICY "employees_own_orders" ON public.orders
  FOR SELECT USING (
    employee_id IN (
      SELECT id FROM public.employees WHERE auth_user_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );
-- Wholesalers can see orders for their products
CREATE POLICY "wholesalers_own_orders" ON public.orders
  FOR SELECT USING (
    wholesaler_id IN (
      SELECT id FROM public.wholesalers WHERE user_id = auth.uid()
    )
  );
-- Service role for inserts/updates (through API routes)
API Routes to Create
Route	Method	Purpose
app/api/orders/create/route.js	POST	Employee sends a request
app/api/orders/[id]/route.js	PATCH	Update order status (accept/reject/pack/dispatch/receive)
app/api/orders/list/route.js	GET	List orders (filtered by role: employee or wholesaler)
Order Status Lifecycle
Employee sends request
Wholesaler accepts
Wholesaler rejects (+ reason)
Wholesaler marks
Wholesaler marks
Wholesaler marks
Employee marks
Auto-complete
pending
accepted
rejected
in_production
packed
dispatched
received
completed
